    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0221" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/1880: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. William Phillips,
                        Personal Representative of President Roosevelt in India, to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-03-24T17:00:00+06:30">March 24, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>237. Viceroy has expressed his willingness to receive delegation of leaders who
                    recently met in Bombay (reference Ambassador Phillip’s recent telegram from
                        Bombay).<anchor n="35" xml:id="d228-f1"/> Competent observers here predict
                    that Viceroy will object [<hi rendition="#italic">reject?</hi>] leaders request
                    for interview with Gandhi and that such rejection will further accentuate the
                    already intense anti-British feeling in the country.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
